# Hard times as chains (phase 7, the h7_ lines): one tells of a theft, a beating, an arrest, a death, a raid, a
# stranger or a deed, or of their own want; the other answers as they are (crime.answer, loss.answer, road.answer,
# want.answer, stranger.answer, deed.answer: by role, means, traits, age and how they are today); and the first answers
# that in turn (the *.close concepts), knowing how it was taken: each answer remembers its stance for the pair for half
# an hour (pair.mem.h7_said), and the close is chosen by that stance and the closer's own facts. A chain's later beats
# always take their best tier, so every answer is keyed to the kind of thing it answers (topic.kind, or pair.mem.wn for
# the want openers), and every close to a stance.

############################################################################ Crime: openers (talk.crime: theft, assault, arrest)

rule h7_cr_open_theft
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft
say Have you heard? #topic.victim# was robbed. | #topic.victim#'s been robbed, they're saying. | Somebody had #topic.victim#'s purse. | There's a #thief# about. #topic.victim# found out the hard way. | #topic.victim# came home to their things gone.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_assault
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=assault
say #topic.victim# was beaten. In the street. | Somebody set on #topic.victim#. | Did you hear about #topic.victim#? Knocked down and kicked. | They hurt #topic.victim#. Badly, I heard.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_arrest
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=arrest
say #watch.capitalize# took #topic.subject#. | They've put #topic.subject# in #gaol#. | #topic.subject#'s been arrested. #topic.where# took them. | Did you see? #topic.subject#, marched off by #watch#.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_guard
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say I've been on #topic.victim#'s business all day. Nothing. | If you hear anything about #topic.victim#, you tell me. | We're looking for whoever did #topic.victim#. Seen anyone odd? | Another one for the book. #topic.victim#.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_guard_arrest
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=arrest self.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say We brought #topic.subject# in. Didn't go quietly. | #topic.subject#'s in #gaol#. Don't ask me what for. You'll hear. | #topic.where# took #topic.subject#. Clean work, for once. | #topic.subject#'s in the cells and swearing at the walls.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_rich
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft self.wealth=rich
cooldown 1d
say What do we pay #watch# for? #topic.victim#, robbed! | I've had the locks changed. After #topic.victim#. All of them. | It'll be someone from outside. It always is. Poor #topic.victim#. | A #thief# in our street. One feels quite exposed.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_poor
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say #topic.victim#'s been robbed. They'll be looking at folk like me now. | Robbed #topic.victim#? They had something to rob, then. | Somebody got #topic.victim#. Not me, before you ask. | #topic.victim#'s robbed. Watch them all look at my paws.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_robbed_too
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft self.robbed=yes
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say #topic.victim# too? They had me only days ago. | First me, now #topic.victim#. Same #thief#, I'll swear it. | They robbed #topic.victim# as well. Who's next on the list? | #topic.victim#. Like me. Does #watch# even care?
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_nervy
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.temper=nervy
cooldown 1d
say #topic.victim#! That's practically on our doorstep! | I heard about #topic.victim# and I haven't stopped shaking. | What if they come back? For #topic.victim#? For us? | #topic.victim#. I knew it. I knew something would happen.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_old
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.stage=old
cooldown 1d
say #topic.victim#. In my day, the whole street would've chased them down. | Sixty years in this town and I've never seen it so bad. Poor #topic.victim#. | They got #topic.victim#. Nobody looks out for anyone now. | #topic.victim#. Ah. Forty years ago I'd have had them by the scruff.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_devout
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say I prayed for #topic.victim# this morning. | Somebody did wrong by #topic.victim#. The gods saw it. | #topic.victim#, of all folk. A chapel-goer! | There's wickedness in this town. Look at #topic.victim#.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_dry
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft self.humour=dry
cooldown 1d
say Somebody robbed #topic.victim#. I hope they wiped their paws. | #topic.victim#'s been relieved of their goods. Very relieving. | A #thief# took #topic.victim#'s things. They'll be disappointed. | #topic.victim# was robbed. At least someone's in work.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_short
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault self.temper=short
cooldown 1d
say If I get my paws on whoever did #topic.victim#... | #topic.victim#! In broad day! And #watch# drinking somewhere! | Whoever did #topic.victim# walks about free. It makes my blood boil. | #topic.victim#. I'm so angry I could bite something.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_sump
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft|assault here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
cooldown 1d
say #topic.victim#'s been done. They'll be down here looking by noon. | They'll blame the Sump for #topic.victim#. Watch. | Not one of ours did #topic.victim#. We'd have heard. | #watch# will kick in a few Sump doors over #topic.victim#. Ours first.
then other: crime.answer

rule h7_cr_open_someone
when concept=talk.crime topic.kind=theft topic.subject=someone self.honesty=sly
cooldown 1d
say Nobody saw a thing, with #topic.victim#. Funny, that. | Robbed, and not a whisker seen. Somebody's good. | #topic.victim#'s things walked off by themselves, it seems. | Whoever did #topic.victim# is better at it than most. I'd almost admire it.
then other: crime.answer

############################################################################ Crime: answers (self is the one answering)

rule h7_cr_ans_any
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault
say Gods. Poor #topic.victim#. | That's a bad business. | I heard. It's everywhere. | Nobody's safe any more. | And in daylight, too, I'll bet.
remember pair: h7_said=sorry 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_any_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest
say Well. That's them done for. | I'd not want to be #topic.subject# tonight. | So they caught someone, for once. | There's always more to it than you hear.
remember pair: h7_said=shrug 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_guard
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.role=guard
say We're on it. We're always on it. | I've been asking all morning. Nobody saw a thing. They never do. | Leave it with #watch#. Don't go playing guard yourself. | If anyone knows anything, tell me. I'll keep your name out.
remember pair: h7_said=duty 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_guard_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest self.role=guard
say And they'll stay there till the magistrate's had a look. | I held the door. They bit #topic.where#. | Don't feel sorry for them. You don't know what they did. | That's one. There's more.
remember pair: h7_said=duty_arrest 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_rich
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.wealth=rich
say Flog them, when they're caught. In the square. | They should hang a few. The rest would learn. | I'll have a wolf on the gate from now on. Two wolves. | One pays a fortune in levies for this?
remember pair: h7_said=hang 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_rich_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest self.wealth=rich
say Good. Let them make an example. | One hopes the magistrate isn't soft. | Splendid. The streets feel safer already. | Keep them in. Keep them all in.
remember pair: h7_said=hang 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_poor
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Hungry, I'd bet. Whoever did it. | I can't say I blame them. Don't look at me like that. | When a wolf's starving, a purse looks like supper. | Robbing the comfortable. Some would call it sharing.
remember pair: h7_said=pity 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_poor_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Poor sod. There'll be nobody to speak up for them. | The rich steal more and nobody takes them. | Somebody'll go hungry with them in #gaol#. | They take our sort. Never theirs.
remember pair: h7_said=pity_arrest 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_hungry
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.wealth=poor|destitute self.hungry=yes
say I've thought about it. Don't tell anyone. I've thought about it. | My belly says good luck to them. My head says shame. | If they took bread, I'd hold the door. | I'm too hungry to be shocked.
remember pair: h7_said=pity 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_short
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.temper=short
say Let me find them. Just let me. | String them up. I'll bring the rope. | And #watch# sitting on their tails! | That makes me want to break something.
remember pair: h7_said=hang 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_nervy
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.temper=nervy
say Don't. I'll not sleep now. | Was it near here? How near? | I knew it. I knew it'd come to this. | Oh, gods. Oh, gods. My door doesn't even lock properly.
remember pair: h7_said=fear 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_robbed
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.robbed=yes
priority 1
say Same as me. Same as me! | Join the club. Nobody wants to be in it. | Now will #watch# listen? Now? | I know just how they feel. Sick. Sick and stupid.
remember pair: h7_said=same 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_devout
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.piety=devout
say I'll pray for #topic.victim#. And for whoever did it. | The gods will settle it. In their time. | There's a wolf out there with a heavy soul tonight. | I'll light a candle for #topic.victim# on Restday.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_devout_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest self.piety=devout
say I'll pray they repent in there. | The gods forgive. Magistrates don't. | Somebody should take them a blessing, at least. | We're all a step from #gaol#, if the gods look away.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_dry
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.humour=dry
say Robbing #topic.victim#. That's ambition. | Well, it's one way to share the wealth. | Lucky #thief#. I've been trying to get rid of my things for years. | I'll put a sign on my door. Nothing worth it here.
remember pair: h7_said=joke 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_merry
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.humour=merry
say Ha! Hope they took the ugly chair too. | Somebody's having a grand day. Not #topic.victim#. | Oh, no. Oh, that's terrible. Did they take the goose? | Ha. Sorry. Sorry. It's not funny. It's a bit funny.
remember pair: h7_said=joke 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_merry_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest self.humour=merry
say Ha! Somebody's having a worse day than me, then. | Free bed and board. There's worse ways to spend a week. | Ha. I'll bet they went kicking.
remember pair: h7_said=joke 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_warm
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.warmth=warm
say Is #topic.victim# all right? Should we go round? | I'll take them something. Soup. | Poor #topic.victim#. They'll need folk about them. | Has anyone sat with #topic.victim#?
remember pair: h7_said=care 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_cold
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.warmth=cold
say Should've locked their door. | Happens. | Not my business. | They'll live.
remember pair: h7_said=cold 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_old
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.stage=old
say In my day we'd have known who it was by supper. | There was a wolf like that when I was a pup. Hanged at the crossroads. | It's always been so. You just hear it more now. | I've been robbed three times in my life. You get over it. Mostly.
remember pair: h7_said=past 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_young
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.stage=young
say Will they come to our house? | I'd bite them! Right on the tail! | Is #topic.victim# all right? | Why did they do it?
remember pair: h7_said=pup 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_young_arrest
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=arrest self.stage=young
say Will they put them in a cage? | Did they fight? I'd have fought. | Can I go and look at #gaol#?
remember pair: h7_said=pup 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_sly
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.honesty=sly
say Hm. Wonder where they'll sell it. | Clever. Nobody saw? Very clever. | What did they get, do you know? Exactly? | #topic.victim# had a lot more than they let on, then.
remember pair: h7_said=sly 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_merchant
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft self.role=merchant
say A stall's next. Mark me. | I'll be sleeping on my stock. | Thieves are worse than bad weather for trade. | I've lost more to light paws than to bad debts.
remember pair: h7_said=fear 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_healer
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=assault self.job=healer
say I was up with #topic.victim# half the night. | I've seen to them. They'll mend. Slowly. | Whoever did it knew where to kick. | I'll go back this evening. They're not to get up.
remember pair: h7_said=mend 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_mourning
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 1
say I can't think about it. Not this week. | Everything's bad news this week. | I've no room left for more sorrow. | Things. They're only things. I know that now.
remember pair: h7_said=grief 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_sump
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft|assault here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
say And they'll blame us. Watch them. | Not one of ours. We'd have heard. | Up the hill, that's news. Down here it's the weather. | They'll come kicking our doors in for it.
remember pair: h7_said=blame 30m
then other: crime.close

rule h7_cr_ans_heights
when concept=crime.answer topic.kind=theft here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=heights self.wealth=rich|comfortable
say One will speak to the captain. Personally. | Was it someone from below, do they think? | Dreadful. One's own servants, quite possibly. | The city's going to ruin.
remember pair: h7_said=hang 30m
then other: crime.close

############################################################################ Crime: closes (self opened; pair.mem.h7_said says how it was taken)

rule h7_cr_close_any
when concept=crime.close
say Aye. Well. | Bad times. | Keep your door shut. | Mind how you go.

rule h7_cr_close_sorry
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=sorry
say Aye. Bad business. | It could be any of us. | I'll go round later. | Poor soul.

rule h7_cr_close_shrug
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=shrug
say Aye. | We'll hear soon enough. | Hm. We'll see. | So it goes.

rule h7_cr_close_duty
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=duty
say I'll keep my ears open. | Find them, then. | You always say that. | Do. Please.

rule h7_cr_close_duty_short
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=duty self.temper=short
say On it? You're stood here talking to me. | Then get off it and find them. | Leave it with you? I'd sooner leave it with the cat.

rule h7_cr_close_duty_arrest
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=duty_arrest
say Good. Keep them there. | Well done, then. | Was it them, though, truly? | I'll sleep easier.

rule h7_cr_close_hang
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=hang
say Hanging's a hard cure. | Hanging won't mend anything. | Steady. | That's strong.

rule h7_cr_close_hang_poor
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=hang self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Easy said from a full belly. | And when it's a hungry pup? Hang them too? | They'd hang me for less. | You'd want the rope for half this street.

rule h7_cr_close_hang_devout
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=hang self.piety=devout
say The gods judge. Not us. | That's not justice. That's anger. | Pray on that before you say it again.

rule h7_cr_close_pity
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=pity
say Hungry's no excuse. | Don't let #watch# hear you say that. | Maybe. Still wrong. | I suppose. I suppose.

rule h7_cr_close_pity_rich
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=pity|pity_arrest self.wealth=rich
say There's always honest work. | That's dangerous talk. | Then they should apply to the parish. | One gives to the chapel for exactly this.

rule h7_cr_close_pity_poor
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=pity|pity_arrest self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Aye. It's not hard to see how. | I know. Gods, I know. | We've all stood at that door. | Hush. But aye.

rule h7_cr_close_pity_arrest
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=pity_arrest
say Maybe. Still, the law's the law. | Aye. It's always our sort. | They did something, though. They must have.

rule h7_cr_close_fear
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=fear
say Bolt the door and you'll be fine. | Don't fret. Lightning doesn't strike twice. | Stay with us tonight, if you like. | It'll pass. These things pass.

rule h7_cr_close_fear_dry
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=fear self.humour=dry
say Cheer up. They'll probably rob someone richer. | You're safe. You've nothing anyone wants. | Sleep with a pan by the bed. Hit anything that moves. Except me.

rule h7_cr_close_same
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=same
say Then you know. | Did they ever find yours? | Gods, I'd forgotten. I'm sorry. | We should go to #watch# together.

rule h7_cr_close_pray
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=pray
say Pray for me while you're at it. | If the gods are listening. | Aye. And for all of us. | Prayers are well and good. A bolt's better.

rule h7_cr_close_joke
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=joke
say That's not funny. | Ha. Don't. | You're terrible. | Wicked. Wicked and right.

rule h7_cr_close_joke_short
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=joke self.temper=short
say It's not a joke. | Laugh, then. Laugh when it's you. | I don't find that funny at all.

rule h7_cr_close_care
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=care
say I'll come with you. | That's kind. Take bread, too. | Let's go round this evening. | You're a good soul.

rule h7_cr_close_care_cold
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=care self.warmth=cold
say Do what you like. | They've family for that. | Suit yourself.

rule h7_cr_close_cold
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=cold
say That's hard, even for you. | Hm. Charming. | I'll remember that, when it's your door.

rule h7_cr_close_past
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=past
say Times change. | Maybe so. | Things were simpler then, I suppose.

rule h7_cr_close_pup
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=pup
say They'll be all right. Don't you fret. | Hush, now. Nobody's coming to ours. | No biting anybody, mind. | Never you mind. Run along.

rule h7_cr_close_sly
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=sly
say You'd know, would you? | I don't like the way you said that. | Funny thing to ask. | Hm. I'll keep my purse closer.

rule h7_cr_close_mend
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=mend
say Thank the gods you were there. | Give them my best. | You're a good sort.

rule h7_cr_close_grief
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=grief
say Of course. Forgive me. | I'm sorry. I forgot. | I shouldn't have said. Not this week.

rule h7_cr_close_blame
when concept=crime.close pair.mem.h7_said=blame
say Nobody's blaming you. | They'll not, this time. | Aye. They always do.

############################################################################ Loss: openers (talk.life, a death in town; talk.news, one's own)

rule h7_ls_open
when concept=talk.life topic.kind=death
say #topic.subject# died. | The bell was for #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject#'s gone. Last night. | #topic.subject#'s to be buried tomorrow. | Did you hear about #topic.subject#? Gone.
then other: loss.answer

rule h7_ls_open_old
when concept=talk.life topic.kind=death self.stage=old
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject#. I knew them when they were a pup. | Another one. They keep going before me. | #topic.subject#'s gone. I remember them at their first festival. | That's #topic.subject# gone. I'll be next, mark me.
then other: loss.answer

rule h7_ls_open_priest
when concept=talk.life topic.kind=death self.job=priest
cooldown 1d
say I'll say the words over #topic.subject# tomorrow. | I was with #topic.subject# at the last. | #topic.subject# is with the Bright One now. | I've #topic.subject#'s burial and two more this week.
then other: loss.answer

rule h7_ls_open_mourning
when concept=talk.life topic.kind=death self.mourning=kin|friend
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say And #topic.subject# now too. I can't. | Another one. As if this week weren't enough. | #topic.subject#. I've only just stopped crying. | Everyone's going. Everyone.
then other: loss.answer

rule h7_ls_open_dry
when concept=talk.life topic.kind=death self.humour=dry self.mourning=no
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject#'s died. Owed me a penny, too. I'll let it go. | #topic.subject#. Gone and missed the rent day. Clever. | They're burying #topic.subject#. They'd have hated the fuss. | #topic.subject# never could stand a queue. Went early.
then other: loss.answer

rule h7_ls_open_poor
when concept=talk.life topic.kind=death self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject#'s gone, and nothing to bury them with. | #topic.subject#. The parish'll do it. Plain box. | They'll put #topic.subject# in the paupers' row. Same as we'll go. | #topic.subject# died. Cold and an empty pot, I'd bet.
then other: loss.answer

rule h7_ls_open_news
when concept=talk.news topic.kind=loss
priority 1
say I've lost someone. This week. | We buried one of ours. I keep thinking I'll see them. | I've had bad news. The worst sort. | You'll hear it anyway. We've had a death.
then other: loss.answer

############################################################################ Loss: answers (topic.kind=death, someone in town; topic.kind=loss, the teller's own)

rule h7_ls_ans_any
when concept=loss.answer
say Ah, no. | That's hard news. | I hadn't heard. I'm sorry. | Rest them.
remember pair: h7_said=sorry 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_own
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=loss
say Oh, I'm so sorry. | I'd no idea. I'm so sorry. | That's hard. Gods, that's hard. | Is there anything I can do?
remember pair: h7_said=sorry 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_warm
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=loss self.warmth=warm
say Oh, #pet#. Come here. | I'll bring food round. Don't argue. | Whatever you need. Anything. | I'm so sorry. Sit with me a while.
remember pair: h7_said=care 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_warm_death
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=death self.warmth=warm
say Oh, their poor family. I'll take something round. | Who's seeing to the family? | I'll sit with them tonight, if they'd like.
remember pair: h7_said=kind 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_cold
when concept=loss.answer self.warmth=cold
say Everyone goes. | Mm. These things happen. | Well. That's that.
remember pair: h7_said=cold 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_cold_death
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=death self.warmth=cold
say Hardly knew them. | Everyone goes. | Mm.
remember pair: h7_said=cold 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_devout
when concept=loss.answer self.piety=devout
say They're with the Bright One now. | I'll pray for them tonight. | The gods keep them. | There's a light gone out, and another lit somewhere.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_old
when concept=loss.answer self.stage=old
say They go so fast now. One a season. | I've buried more friends than I have left. | At my age you stop counting. You don't stop missing. | Gone before me. That's not the right order.
remember pair: h7_said=old 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_young
when concept=loss.answer self.stage=young
say Are they coming back? | Will they be cold in #grave#? | Is that why everyone's sad? | I don't want anyone to die.
remember pair: h7_said=young 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_dry
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=death self.humour=dry other.mourning=no
say Well. They always said they'd go first. | Gone to a better place. Couldn't be much worse than here. | Lucky them. No more winters. | Death and levies, and they've beaten the levies.
remember pair: h7_said=joke 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_poor
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=death self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Who'll pay for the burying? | At least they're warm now. Wherever they are. | One less mouth, they'll say at the big houses. | It's always our sort that go first.
remember pair: h7_said=poor 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_mourning
when concept=loss.answer self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 1
say Not another. I can't hold another. | I know how it sits. Gods, I know. | I've no tears left. I'm sorry. | We're all burying someone this season.
remember pair: h7_said=grief 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_widowed
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=loss self.widowed=yes
say It doesn't get easier. It gets quieter. | You'll talk to them. Everyone does. | I still set two cups. Don't tell anyone. | The first winter's the worst.
remember pair: h7_said=grief 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_short
when concept=loss.answer self.temper=short
say Why do the good ones go? Why? | It's not fair. None of it's fair. | Don't. I'll hit a wall. | Gods curse it.
remember pair: h7_said=angry 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_priest
when concept=loss.answer self.job=priest
say I'll say the words. Good words. | Come to the chapel, after. We'll light one together. | Grief is love with nowhere to go. Give it somewhere. | They were loved. That's what I'll say, because it's true.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_healer
when concept=loss.answer topic.kind=death self.job=healer
say I should've been called sooner. | I did what I could. It wasn't enough. | There was nothing in the jar for that. | I'll not sleep tonight.
remember pair: h7_said=healer 30m
then other: loss.close

rule h7_ls_ans_rich
when concept=loss.answer self.wealth=rich
say How dreadful. I'll send something. | One must pay one's respects. | I'll see the stone's paid for. | Such a shame. Did they leave the family anything?
remember pair: h7_said=rich 30m
then other: loss.close

############################################################################ Loss: closes

rule h7_ls_close_any
when concept=loss.close
say Aye. | Thank you. | It's a hard week. | Rest them.

rule h7_ls_close_care
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=care
say Thank you. Truly. | You're good to me. | I'd like that. | I'll not argue. Not today.

rule h7_ls_close_kind
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=kind
say That's good of you. | They'd be glad of it. | I'll come with you.

rule h7_ls_close_cold
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=cold
say Is that all? | Well, I knew them. | Gods, you're a stone. | Thank you for nothing.

rule h7_ls_close_pray
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=pray
say Say one for me too. | I hope so. | If anyone's listening. | Thank you. That helps. A little.

rule h7_ls_close_pray_short
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=pray self.piety=ordinary self.temper=short
say The gods took them. They can keep their light. | Pray if you like. I'll drink. | Don't tell me about the gods today.

rule h7_ls_close_old
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=old
say Don't you go anywhere. | You'll outlast us all. | Then tell me about them. The old ones. | Aye. You've seen more of it than most.

rule h7_ls_close_young
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=young
say Hush, pup. Come here. | It's sad, pup. That's all. It's just sad. | You'll understand when you're older. Come here. | It's all right. It's all right.

rule h7_ls_close_joke
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=joke
say Ha. They'd have laughed at that. | Don't. I'll laugh at the burial. | That's dreadful. Say it again. | You're awful.

rule h7_ls_close_poor
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=poor
say We'll pass a hat. | The parish, I suppose. | Aye. It's always us. | We'll go the same way.

rule h7_ls_close_angry
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=angry
say I know. I know. | Hit the wall, then. I'll hold your coat. | Curse it with you. | Aye. Curse it.

rule h7_ls_close_rich
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=rich
say That's... generous. | Send bread, not flowers. They'll need feeding. | Aye. Well. Thank you.

rule h7_ls_close_grief
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=grief
say I know. I'm sorry. | We'll get through it. Somehow. | Come here. Both of us, then.

rule h7_ls_close_healer
when concept=loss.close pair.mem.h7_said=healer
say It's not your fault. | You did all anyone could. | Nobody blames you.

############################################################################ The road: openers (talk.bandits, talk.caravan raided)

rule h7_rd_open
when concept=talk.bandits topic.kind=raided
say #bandits.capitalize# again. They had the #topic.where# carts. | The road to #topic.where#'s been robbed again. | They raided a caravan out of #topic.where#. | Nothing's coming from #topic.where# this week. Robbed.
then other: road.answer

rule h7_rd_open_camp
when concept=talk.bandits topic.kind=camp
say There's a camp out by #topic.where#. #bandits.capitalize#. | Somebody saw fires out by #topic.where#. | They're camped out by #topic.where#, bold as you like. | Stay off the road past #topic.where#.
then other: road.answer

rule h7_rd_open_caravan
when concept=talk.caravan topic.kind=raided
say The #topic.where# caravan never made it. | They hit the carts from #topic.where#. | We'll get nothing from #topic.where# this week. | Robbed. The whole #topic.where# run.
then other: road.answer

rule h7_rd_open_merchant
when concept=talk.bandits|talk.caravan topic.kind=raided self.role=merchant
cooldown 1d
say There goes my stock. On the #topic.where# road. | That was my order on those carts. | I'll have nothing to sell by market day. | Another raid. I'll have to put the prices up.
then other: road.answer

rule h7_rd_open_travelling
when concept=talk.bandits topic.kind=raided|camp self.travelling=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say I'm on that road tomorrow. That very road. | I've to go out past #topic.where#. Gods help me. | I'd hoped to be away by dawn. Now I don't know. | Is there another way? Any other way?
then other: road.answer

rule h7_rd_open_guard
when concept=talk.bandits topic.kind=raided|camp self.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say They want riders for #topic.where#. Volunteers. | Captain says we're not to go past the milestones. Whatever happens. | We've twelve wolves and a lame horse. Against that. | I'd go after them. If they let me.
then other: road.answer

rule h7_rd_open_poor
when concept=talk.bandits|talk.caravan topic.kind=raided self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say They robbed the carts. Bread'll be dear again. | Robbers took the #topic.where# load. Guess who pays. | The rich lose a cart, we lose supper. | Another raid. Another penny on the loaf.
then other: road.answer

############################################################################ The road: answers

rule h7_rd_ans_any
when concept=road.answer
say Not again. | Gods keep the carters. | It's getting worse. | The roads were never safe. | Somebody ought to do something.
remember pair: h7_said=shrug 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_guard
when concept=road.answer self.role=guard
say We can't be everywhere. | The road's not ours. The walls are. | Give us horses and we'll ride. | I'd go. Tonight. If the captain let me.
remember pair: h7_said=duty 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_merchant
when concept=road.answer self.role=merchant
say Then prices go up. Don't look at me. | I'll be selling turnips and hope. | Guards cost more than goods, now. | My next order's sitting in a yard somewhere, too frightened to move.
remember pair: h7_said=trade 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_carter
when concept=road.answer self.job=carter
say I'll not drive that road. Not for double. | I know those carters. I'll go and see them. | That's my road. That's my road! | Next run's mine. Gods.
remember pair: h7_said=fear_road 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_travelling
when concept=road.answer self.travelling=yes
priority 1
say And I've to go out there. | Don't tell me that. I leave at dawn. | Then I'm walking with the carts. Close. | I'll go the long way. Three days more.
remember pair: h7_said=fear_road 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_poor
when concept=road.answer self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Nothing of mine on it. I'll sleep sound. | They'll put the price of it on our bread. | Robbers robbing the rich. Hard to cry. | Let the Houses guard their own carts.
remember pair: h7_said=poor 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_rich
when concept=road.answer self.wealth=rich
say Someone must raise a troop. One would contribute. | It's the Houses' business. Let them see to it. | How tiresome. There was wine on that cart. | One's agent will have to find another way.
remember pair: h7_said=rich 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_nervy
when concept=road.answer self.temper=nervy
say What if they come here? Into town? | I knew it. I knew it was coming. | Don't. I'll dream about it. | They're getting closer. Aren't they?
remember pair: h7_said=fear 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_short
when concept=road.answer self.temper=short
say Give me a spear and twelve good wolves. | Burn them out. That's all they understand. | And #watch# sitting on the walls! | I'm sick of it. Sick of it!
remember pair: h7_said=fight 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_old
when concept=road.answer self.stage=old
say In my day we hanged them at the crossroads. | It was worse when I was young. Truly. | Bandits come and go, like the weather. | They'll move on in the spring. They always do.
remember pair: h7_said=old 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_devout
when concept=road.answer self.piety=devout
say I'll pray for the carters. | Gods keep the road. | We'll pray for them on Restday. All of us. | There's evil on the roads this season.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_ambitious
when concept=road.answer self.drive=ambitious|restless self.stage=adult
say Someone's going to make good money guarding carts. | Whoever clears that road will be a name. | I'd go. With the right pay. | That's a chance, if you look at it right.
remember pair: h7_said=chance 30m
then other: road.close

rule h7_rd_ans_dry
when concept=road.answer self.humour=dry
say Good. Fewer carts, less traffic. | They'll be wanting a stall at the market next. | Somebody's trade is booming, then. | At least they're working.
remember pair: h7_said=joke 30m
then other: road.close

############################################################################ The road: closes

rule h7_rd_close_any
when concept=road.close
say Aye. Bad times. | Gods keep them. | Let's hope it passes. | We'll see.

rule h7_rd_close_duty
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=duty
say Then what are you for? | So we sit and wait. | Ask again. Ask louder. | Walls don't feed us.

rule h7_rd_close_trade
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=trade
say You'd put them up anyway. | Lovely. Dearer everything. | Then we go without. Again. | Blame the road. Always the road.

rule h7_rd_close_fear_road
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=fear_road
say Go in daylight. All of it. | Go with others. Never alone. | Gods keep you. | Stay, if you can.

rule h7_rd_close_fear
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=fear
say They'll not come here. Not with the walls. | Calm yourself. They're miles off. | Bolt your door, if it helps.

rule h7_rd_close_poor
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=poor
say It's not the Houses who'll go hungry. | Aye. Sound sleep's the one thing we've got. | Ha. Fair. | And who pays? We do.

rule h7_rd_close_rich
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=rich
say Wine. Gods help us. | Raise one, then. You've the coin. | The carters had pups, you know. | Tiresome. Aye.

rule h7_rd_close_fight
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=fight
say And who'd follow you? | Twelve wolves. Name eleven. | Burn and be burnt. | Calm yourself.

rule h7_rd_close_old
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=old
say Maybe so. | I hope you're right. | Times change, and not for the better.

rule h7_rd_close_pray
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=pray
say Pray harder. | And a spear, with the prayer. | Pray they come home. | Aye. Gods keep them.

rule h7_rd_close_chance
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=chance
say A chance to die. | Go on, then. I'll watch. | Big talk. | Someone will. Not you.

rule h7_rd_close_joke
when concept=road.close pair.mem.h7_said=joke
say That's grim. | Ha. Don't. | You'd joke at your own wake. | Very funny.

############################################################################ Want: openers (one in want tells or asks; pair.mem.wn says what)

rule h7_wn_open_loan
when concept=talk.friends|talk.smalltalk self.wealth=destitute other.wealth=comfortable|rich pair.band=friends|family|acquaintances self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
cooldown 3d
say I hate to ask. Could you lend me a little? | Just till Restday. A few pennies. I'll pay it back. | I'm short. Very short. Could you see your way? | I've never asked you for anything. I'm asking now.
remember pair: wn=loan 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_hungry
when concept=talk.friends|talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.hungry=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say I've not eaten since yesterday morning. | You've not got a crust? Anything? | I'm that hungry I could eat the cobbles. | Is it wrong to steal bread? Asking for a friend. The friend is me.
remember pair: wn=hungry 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_dole
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.on_dole=yes self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say I'm on #dole# now. You'll have seen me in the line. | Two hours for the parish loaf, and it was yesterday's. | Never thought I'd queue for bread. | The priest knows my name now. From the line.
remember pair: wn=dole 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_owes
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends self.owes=yes self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say The lender came round. With a friend. A big friend. | I owe more than I own. Don't tell anyone. | I can't pay. I can't. What do I do? | If I go missing, the lender's had me.
remember pair: wn=owes 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_homeless
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.friends|talk.day self.homeless=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say I've nowhere to sleep tonight. | They put my things out in the street. | I've been sleeping in the market. Under a stall. | You've not got a corner? A floor? Anything?
remember pair: wn=homeless 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_failing
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.work self.business=failing self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say The business is finished. I'll be selling the shelves next. | Nobody's buying, and the rent's due. | I've stock rotting and no coin for bread. | I'll be on #dole# by the month's end. Me. With a trade.
remember pair: wn=failing 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_hurt
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends self.injured=bad self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
cooldown 12h
say I can't work like this. And if I don't work, I don't eat. | Look at my arm. How do I lift a sack with that? | The healer wants paying. With what? | I'll lose my place if I'm off a week.
remember pair: wn=hurt 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_robbed
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends self.robbed=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say They took the little I had. All of it. | Robbed. And I'd nothing to start with. | The rent was in that purse. The rent! | Whoever took it, I hope they choke on it.
remember pair: wn=robbed 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_old_poor
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day self.stage=old self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say A lifetime's work and nothing to show. Nothing. | I'm too old for the work and too young to die. | My pups are grown and gone, and the pot's empty. | When I can't work, I'll go to the chapel steps. That's all there is.
remember pair: wn=old 30m
then other: want.answer

rule h7_wn_open_parent
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.family|talk.friends self.parent=yes self.age<=45 self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say The pups went to bed hungry again. | I gave mine my supper. They didn't know. | How do you tell a pup there's no more? | My little one asked why we're poor. I'd no answer.
remember pair: wn=pups 30m
then other: want.answer

############################################################################ Want: answers (self is the one answering)

rule h7_wn_ans_any
when concept=want.answer
say I'm sorry. Truly. | That's hard. | Gods. What'll you do? | It'll turn. It has to. | That's no way to live.
remember pair: h7_said=sorry 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_rich_warm
when concept=want.answer self.wealth=rich|comfortable self.warmth=warm
say Here. Take this. No, don't count it. | Come and eat with us tonight. And tomorrow. | I'll see you right. Don't argue with me. | How much do you need? Tell me true.
remember pair: h7_said=give 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_rich_cold
when concept=want.answer self.wealth=rich self.warmth=cold
say I'm sure the parish can help. | One can't help everyone, you understand. | Have you tried finding work? | I don't carry coin about with me.
remember pair: h7_said=refuse 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_rich
when concept=want.answer self.wealth=rich
say A few pennies. Here. Don't mention it. | Perhaps I could find you some work. Something. | Here. Take this, and don't argue. | You should have come to me sooner. Here.
remember pair: h7_said=give 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_comfortable
when concept=want.answer self.wealth=comfortable
say I can spare a little. Not much. Here. | I've a loaf at home. It's yours. | We're not flush ourselves, but here. | Here. It's not much, but it's yours.
remember pair: h7_said=give 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_poor
when concept=want.answer self.wealth=poor|destitute
say I'd give you half if I had a whole. | We're in the same boat, you and I. Both bailing. | I've a turnip. A small one. It's yours. | If I had it, it'd be yours.
remember pair: h7_said=same 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_sly
when concept=want.answer self.honesty=sly pair.mem.wn=loan|hungry|owes|failing|robbed|dole
say I could lend. At a fair rate. Very fair. | I might know someone who pays for odd jobs. Don't ask what. | What have you got to sell? | There's always a way. If you're not fussy.
remember pair: h7_said=sly 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_frank
when concept=want.answer self.honesty=frank pair.mem.wn=loan|owes|failing|dole
say You should've come to me before it got this bad. | You've known this was coming. So have I. | I'll help. But you'll listen first. | Pride got you here. Leave it at the door.
remember pair: h7_said=scold 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_devout
when concept=want.answer self.piety=devout
say The chapel feeds anyone who asks. I'll take you. | The gods test the ones they love. | Pray with me. Then we'll find you bread. | The Bright One sees. I'll speak to the chaplain.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_short
when concept=want.answer self.temper=short
say And what do you want me to do about it? | Everyone's got troubles. | Don't look at me. I've my own. | Then do something, don't moan.
remember pair: h7_said=refuse 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_guard
when concept=want.answer self.role=guard pair.mem.wn=hungry|dole|owes|homeless|loan|pups|old|failing
say The captain wants porters at the watch post. It's work. | Don't do anything stupid. I'd have to take you in. | Go to the chapel before dark. Tell them I sent you. | If anyone gives you trouble over it, you send for me.
remember pair: h7_said=duty 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_guard_robbed
when concept=want.answer self.role=guard pair.mem.wn=robbed
say Did you see who took it? Tell me everything. | When was this? Where? | Come by the watch post and we'll write it down.
remember pair: h7_said=ask 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_dry
when concept=want.answer self.humour=dry pair.mem.wn=loan|hungry|dole|owes|failing|robbed|homeless
say Cheer up. You can't get much poorer. | At least you're not rich. All that worry. | Look on the bright side. There isn't one. | Think how thin you'll be.
remember pair: h7_said=joke 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_merchant_failing
when concept=want.answer self.role=merchant self.business=failing
say You and me both. I'm one bad week from the street. | I'd give you credit, if I had stock to give it on. | Nobody's buying. Nobody's eating. It's all one. | I can't help. I can't even help myself.
remember pair: h7_said=same 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_baker
when concept=want.answer self.job=baker|cook pair.mem.wn=hungry|dole|pups|homeless|old|robbed|loan
say There's ends at the back. Come by at dusk. | I've a loaf with a burnt bottom. It's yours. | I'll put something by. Don't tell the others. | Bread I've got. Coin I haven't.
remember pair: h7_said=give 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_healer_hurt
when concept=want.answer self.job=healer pair.mem.wn=hurt
say Come and see me. No charge. Don't argue. | Keep it still, keep it clean, and come to me tomorrow. | I'll see to you. Pay me when you can. Or don't.
remember pair: h7_said=mend 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_healer
when concept=want.answer self.job=healer pair.mem.wn=hungry|pups|dole|homeless
say Eat something before you fall. That's a healer's order. | Hunger's a sickness too. I'll send word to the chapel for you. | Come by mine. There's broth, and nobody counts the bowls.
remember pair: h7_said=give 30m
then other: want.close

rule h7_wn_ans_old
when concept=want.answer self.stage=old
say I've been poorer. It passes. Mostly. | Eat what's there. Don't wait for what isn't. | We ate nettles one winter. Nettles! And lived. | Keep your chin up. And your tail down. Less to bite.
remember pair: h7_said=old 30m
then other: want.close

############################################################################ Want: closes

rule h7_wn_close_any
when concept=want.close
say Aye. | Thank you for listening. | I'll manage. | Somehow.

rule h7_wn_close_give
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=give
say I... thank you. I'll not forget it. | You're too good to me. | I'll pay it back. Every penny. | I don't know what to say.

rule h7_wn_close_give_proud
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=give self.temper=short
say I'll take it. I hate taking it. Thank you. | Don't tell anyone. Please. | I'll pay it back. I will. Don't look at me like that.

rule h7_wn_close_refuse
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=refuse
say Right. Of course. | Forget I said anything. | I'll not ask again. | I see.

rule h7_wn_close_refuse_short
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=refuse self.temper=short
say Easy for you to say. | Keep your coin, then. Choke on it. | I'll remember that.

rule h7_wn_close_same
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=same
say Look at us. | Two of a kind. | We'll get through. Somehow. | At least we've got each other. And nothing else.

rule h7_wn_close_sly
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=sly
say I'm not that desperate. Yet. | What sort of jobs? | Never mind. Never mind. | I'd sooner starve honest.

rule h7_wn_close_scold
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=scold
say I know. I know. | Thank you. I think. | You're right. That's the worst part. | That's not help, that's a sermon.

rule h7_wn_close_pray
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=pray
say Bread first. Then the gods. | I'll go. Thank you. | The gods can test someone else. | If you'd come with me.

rule h7_wn_close_duty
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=duty
say I'll go. Thank you. | I'm not a thief. Not yet. | I'll go before dark. | I might. Thank you.

rule h7_wn_close_ask
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=ask
say It was too quick. I saw nothing. | Last night. By the well. | Everything I had. Everything.

rule h7_wn_close_joke
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=joke
say Ha. Thank you. I think. | That's cruel. And true. | You're no help at all. | I needed that. Gods help me.

rule h7_wn_close_old
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=old
say I'll try. | It had better pass. | Easy said, at your age. | Aye. I suppose you've seen worse.

rule h7_wn_close_mend
when concept=want.close pair.mem.h7_said=mend
say Thank you. I'll come tomorrow. | Bless you. I'll come. | You're a good soul.

############################################################################ Strangers: openers (talk.player; topic.subject is a name they were given, or "that grey stranger")

rule h7_st_open
when concept=talk.player topic.known=yes
say #topic.subject#'s about again. | Look. #topic.subject#. | Look who's back. #topic.subject#. | See #topic.subject# over there?
then other: stranger.answer

rule h7_st_open_unknown
when concept=talk.player topic.known=no
say Never seen #topic.subject# before. Have you? | #topic.subject# just walked in like they own the place. | What do you make of #topic.subject#? | Somebody new. #topic.subject#. Mind them.
then other: stranger.answer

rule h7_st_open_hire
when concept=talk.player world.bandits=near self.wealth=comfortable|rich
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject# looks handy. With the roads as they are. | I'd pay #topic.subject# to see my goods through. | Could #topic.subject# be hired, do you think? | Somebody like #topic.subject# could earn well this season.
then other: stranger.answer

rule h7_st_open_crime
when concept=talk.player world.crime=recent topic.known=no
cooldown 1d
say Thefts in town, and #topic.subject# turns up. | Did #topic.subject# come before or after the robbery? | I'd watch #topic.subject#, with things going missing. | Who saw #topic.subject# come in? With all this thieving?
then other: stranger.answer

rule h7_st_open_guard
when concept=talk.player self.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say I've been told to keep an eye on #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject#. Know anything? | Seen #topic.subject# making trouble? | I like to know who's in my streets. What about #topic.subject#?
then other: stranger.answer

rule h7_st_open_robbed
when concept=talk.player self.robbed=yes
cooldown 12h
say Could #topic.subject# find who robbed me, do you think? | I keep looking at #topic.subject#. Since I was robbed, I look at everyone. | Travellers hear things. #topic.subject# might know who took my things. | Was #topic.subject# about when I was robbed?
then other: stranger.answer

rule h7_st_open_poor
when concept=talk.player self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject# looks like they've coin. More than us. | Would #topic.subject# spare a penny, do you think? | I'd ask #topic.subject# for work. Any work. | Look at #topic.subject#'s boots. I could live a month on those boots.
then other: stranger.answer

############################################################################ Strangers: answers

rule h7_st_ans_any
when concept=stranger.answer
say A traveller. Passing through. | Don't know. Don't care. | Who knows, with travellers. | They look tired. | Let them be.
remember pair: h7_said=shrug 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_guard
when concept=stranger.answer self.role=guard
say I've my eye on them. | They've caused no trouble. Yet. | Came in by the gate. Asked the way. Polite. | If they're trouble, they'll find me.
remember pair: h7_said=duty 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_nervy
when concept=stranger.answer self.temper=nervy
say I don't like them. I don't like any of them. | Don't look at them. They'll see us looking. | Are they armed? They're armed. | Let's go inside.
remember pair: h7_said=fear 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_merchant
when concept=stranger.answer self.role=merchant
say They've coin. Travellers always do. | I'll give them a good price. Good for me. | Ask them what they need. I've everything. | Customers. That's what I see.
remember pair: h7_said=trade 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_warm
when concept=stranger.answer self.warmth=warm
say Someone should give them a hot meal. | They look like they could use a friend. | I'll say good day. It costs nothing. | Poor thing. Far from home.
remember pair: h7_said=kind 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_cold
when concept=stranger.answer self.warmth=cold self.honesty=guarded
say Strangers bring trouble. Always. | I'll keep my door shut. | Don't talk to them. | They'll be gone soon. Good.
remember pair: h7_said=fear 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_ambitious
when concept=stranger.answer self.drive=ambitious|restless
say I'd like to see what they've seen. | I wonder what they earn. Out there. | I could do what they do. | Lucky. Free as the wind.
remember pair: h7_said=envy 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_young
when concept=stranger.answer self.stage=young|adolescent
say Are they a hero? | Have they got a sword? Can I see? | I want to go and talk to them! | Do they fight #bandits#?
remember pair: h7_said=young 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_rich
when concept=stranger.answer self.wealth=rich
say One could find a use for someone like that. | Perhaps they'd take a position. | They look capable. One needs capable. | Ask what they charge.
remember pair: h7_said=hire 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_sly
when concept=stranger.answer self.honesty=sly
say Wonder what's in that pack. | Strangers don't know the prices. Just saying. | Find out what they want. Then sell it. | They'll know things. Things worth knowing.
remember pair: h7_said=trade 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_st_ans_devout
when concept=stranger.answer self.piety=devout
say We were all strangers somewhere once. | The gods send travellers to test us. | I'll pray for their road. | They should come to the chapel. All are welcome.
remember pair: h7_said=kind 30m
then other: stranger.close

############################################################################ Strangers and deeds: closes

rule h7_st_close_any
when concept=stranger.close
say Maybe. | We'll see. | Aye. | Hm.

rule h7_st_close_shrug
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=shrug
say Maybe. | We'll see. | Aye. | Well. There they are.

rule h7_st_close_duty
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=duty
say Good. Keep it on them. | Polite's how they start. | Good to know. | I'll sleep easier.

rule h7_st_close_fear
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=fear
say You're frightened of your own tail. | They're just a traveller. | Calm down. They'll hear you. | Fine. Inside.

rule h7_st_close_fear_nervy
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=fear self.temper=nervy
say You see it too? I'm not mad? | Inside. Now. Quickly. | I said so. I said so.

rule h7_st_close_trade
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=trade
say You'd sell your mother to a traveller. | Don't fleece them. | Money, money. | Go on, then. Before someone else does.

rule h7_st_close_kind
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=kind
say You go and do it, then. | You're soft. | Good of you. | They might bite.

rule h7_st_close_envy
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=envy
say And sleep in ditches? | The wind gets cold. | You'd last a day. | Go, then. Write to us.

rule h7_st_close_young
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=young
say Ha. Maybe, pup. | You'll have to ask them. | Calm down, little one. | One day, maybe.

rule h7_st_close_hire
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=hire
say Everyone can be bought. The question's how dear. | Then ask. | And trust them how? | You'd hire the moon if it'd carry your parcels.

rule h7_st_close_admire
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=admire
say Good. We need more like that. | I'll buy them a drink, if I see them. | Let's hope it's catching. | So say we all.

rule h7_st_close_outdone
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=outdone
say Then ride out yourselves next time. | Sour suits you. | Somebody had to. | Ha. Jealous?

rule h7_st_close_pray
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=pray
say Bless them, aye. | Thank them too. Not just the gods. | The gods and a strong arm. | If you say so.

rule h7_st_close_doubt
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=doubt
say You'd doubt the sun. | Believe what you like. | Ask them, then. | I believe it.

rule h7_st_close_doubt_frank
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=doubt self.honesty=frank
say I know the wolf who saw it. I'd trust them with my life. | You weren't there. Nor was I. But I believe them.

rule h7_st_close_road
when concept=stranger.close pair.mem.h7_said=road
say Aye. If only. | Someone should ask them. | I'd chip in, if somebody asked.

############################################################################ Deeds: openers and answers (talk.deed: topic.subject, topic.deed, topic.nickname)

rule h7_dd_open
when concept=talk.deed
say You'll like this. #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. | Have you heard about #topic.subject#? They #topic.deed#. | Word is #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.deed#.
then other: deed.answer

rule h7_dd_open_nickname
when concept=talk.deed topic.has_nickname=yes
say #topic.nickname#, they call them now. Because they #topic.deed#. | Heard of #topic.nickname#? That's #topic.subject#. They #topic.deed#. | #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. Folk call them #topic.nickname# for it.
then other: deed.answer

rule h7_dd_open_poor
when concept=talk.deed self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. Somebody's luck turned. | #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. Wish they'd come down our street. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. There's hope for some, then. | #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. Not for the likes of us, but still.
then other: deed.answer

rule h7_dd_ans_any
when concept=deed.answer
say Good for them. | That's something, these days. | Did they, now? | Well, well.
remember pair: h7_said=admire 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_doubt
when concept=deed.answer self.honesty=guarded|sly
say Says who? | I'll believe it when I see it. | Funny how nobody saw them do it. | Nobody does that for nothing.
remember pair: h7_said=doubt 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_warm
when concept=deed.answer self.warmth=warm
say Oh, that's lovely. That does my heart good. | There are good folk left, then. | I'd like to shake their paw. | That's the best thing I've heard all week.
remember pair: h7_said=admire 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_guard
when concept=deed.answer self.role=guard
say Doing our job. Better than us, apparently. | Saves us a ride, I suppose. | Hmph. They should've left it to the Watch. | Well. I'll not complain.
remember pair: h7_said=outdone 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_rich
when concept=deed.answer self.wealth=rich
say One should have them to dinner. | Someone like that is worth knowing. | One might find them a position. | How admirable. How useful.
remember pair: h7_said=hire 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_devout
when concept=deed.answer self.piety=devout
say The gods work through such folk. | I'll give thanks on Restday. | That's the Bright One's paw in it. | Bless them. Bless them.
remember pair: h7_said=pray 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_young
when concept=deed.answer self.stage=young|adolescent
say A hero! A real one! | I want to be them when I grow up! | Can we meet them? Please? | Did they have a sword?
remember pair: h7_said=young 30m
then other: stranger.close

rule h7_dd_ans_bandits
when concept=deed.answer world.bandits=near
say Now if they'd do the same for the road. | Ask them to have a go at the #bandits#. | We could use them here. With the road as it is. | Someone like that, and the road might open.
remember pair: h7_said=road 30m
then other: stranger.close

############################################################################ How they're keeping, in hard times (more answers to keeping.sorry and keeping.nod)
# keeping.sorry follows the other's own answer, which is about the worst thing they have (mourning, then a bad
# injury or no home, then a robbery, hunger, want or a failing business, then the dole or debts): each of these
# answers holds only when that is what the other will have spoken of.

rule h7_sorry_healer
when concept=keeping.sorry self.job=healer other.injured=bad other.mourning=no other.homeless=no
say Come by. Let me look at it properly. | Keep it clean and keep it still. I mean it. | That wants a poultice. Tonight. | You're walking on it? Sit down this instant.

rule h7_sorry_guard_robbed
when concept=keeping.sorry self.role=guard other.robbed=yes other.mourning=no other.injured!=bad other.homeless=no other.hungry=no other.wealth!=destitute other.business!=failing
say Tell me everything. Slowly. What, where, when. | We'll find them. Or I'll know why not. | Did you see their face? Their coat? Anything? | Come by the watch post. We'll write it down.

rule h7_sorry_priest_mourning
when concept=keeping.sorry self.job=priest other.mourning=kin|friend other.injured!=bad other.homeless=no
say Come to the chapel tonight. Just to sit. | They're at peace. You're the one I worry for. | Grief's the price of love. You paid it gladly. | I'll come by tomorrow. Leave the door on the latch.

rule h7_sorry_homeless_both
when concept=keeping.sorry self.homeless=yes other.homeless=yes other.mourning=no other.injured!=bad
say There's a dry spot under the granary eaves. Room for two. | Stay near me tonight. It's warmer, two. | The chapel porch, if we're quick. | We'll find somewhere. We always do.

rule h7_sorry_hungry_both
when concept=keeping.sorry self.hungry=yes other.hungry=yes other.mourning=no other.injured!=bad other.homeless=no other.robbed=no
say Me too. My belly's been arguing all day. | We'll find something. Together. | Two empty pots. | Don't talk about it. It makes it worse.

rule h7_sorry_rich_cold_dole
when concept=keeping.sorry self.wealth=rich self.warmth=cold other.on_dole=yes other.mourning=no other.injured!=bad other.robbed=no other.homeless=no
say Well. That's what the parish is for. | One does give to the chapel, you know. | I'm sure it's only temporary. | Hm. Quite.

rule h7_sorry_dole_both
when concept=keeping.sorry self.on_dole=yes other.on_dole=yes other.mourning=no other.injured!=bad other.robbed=no other.homeless=no
say I'll save you a place in the line. | See you at the chapel door, then. | At least the line's good company. | Bring a sack. They've turnips Restday.

rule h7_sorry_owes_both
when concept=keeping.sorry self.owes=yes other.owes=yes other.mourning=no other.injured!=bad other.robbed=no other.homeless=no other.hungry=no other.wealth!=destitute other.business!=failing other.on_dole=no
say Same lender? | We should hide together. Cheaper. | I owe too. We'll go down together. | Don't answer the door. That's my advice.

rule h7_nod_fought_short
when concept=keeping.nod self.temper=short other.fought=yes other.injured!=light
say Who was it? Tell me who. | Did you win, at least? | Next time, call me first. | I'd have finished it for you.

############################################################################ Reactions and barks, in hard times

rule h7_react_theft_poor
when concept=react.theft wealth=poor|destitute
say Good luck to them. ... I never said that. | Run, you fool! Run! | There's a hungry one. | Ha. Not my purse, for once.

rule h7_react_theft_rich
when concept=react.theft wealth=rich
say Stop them! Somebody stop them! Where's the Watch? | Outrageous! In broad day! | My purse. Is it... yes. Thank the gods. | Thief! Guard! Anyone!

rule h7_react_theft_merchant
when concept=react.theft role=merchant
say My stock! Was it my stock? | Watch your stalls! Thief about! | Paws off! Paws off the goods! | That's the third this week!

rule h7_react_theft_nervy
when concept=react.theft temper=nervy
say Oh, gods. Oh, gods. Is everyone all right? | I knew it. I knew today was a bad day. | Somebody do something! Not me! | My heart. My heart.

rule h7_react_fight_old
when concept=react.fight stage=old
say In my day we fought fair. Mostly. | Young fools. Break it up! | I'd have had them both, forty years ago. | Mind my stick! Mind it!

rule h7_react_fight_merchant
when concept=react.fight role=merchant
say Not near the stall! Not near the stall! | Take it outside! This is outside. Take it further! | Who's paying for that? Who's paying? | Mind the goods, you brutes!

rule h7_react_fight_devout
when concept=react.fight piety=devout
say Gods forgive them. Stop! | Peace! In the gods' names, peace! | Brothers! Sisters! Stop! | The Bright One sees you!

rule h7_react_fight_dry
when concept=react.fight humour=dry
say Lovely. Entertainment. | Two pennies on the short one. | Ah. The evening's begun. | Somebody fetch a bucket. Of water. Or ale.

rule h7_react_struck_light
when concept=react.struck injured=light
say Ow! Right. Right! | That'll mark. | You'll pay for that. | Lucky. That was lucky.

rule h7_bark_watch_crime
when concept=bark on_watch=yes world.crime=recent
cooldown 3h
say Keep your purses close, all! | Thieves about. Mind yourselves! | Anyone seen anything, you come to me. | Bolt your doors tonight, folks.

rule h7_bark_watch_bandits
when concept=bark on_watch=yes world.bandits=near here.place=gate
cooldown 3h
say Nobody out past the milestones after dusk! | Travelling? In company only. Hear me? | Gate shuts early tonight. Road's not safe. | Mind the road out there. Mind it well.

rule h7_bark_merchant_bandits
when concept=bark role=merchant world.bandits=near here.place=market
cooldown 6h
say Buy now! Next cart may never come! | Last of the stock till the road's clear! | Prices are the road's fault, not mine! | Get it while there's some to get!

rule h7_bark_destitute_beg
when concept=bark wealth=destitute here.place=street|market|gate|chapel
cooldown 6h
say Spare a penny? Half a penny? | A crust, anyone? For the gods' sake. | Anything at all. Anything. | Bless you. Bless you all. Anyone?

rule h7_bark_destitute_beg_rest
when concept=bark wealth=destitute here.day=rest here.place=chapel|street
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say Restday, friends. A penny for the gods' sake. | Show the gods your kindness. A penny. | Bless you, bless your Restday. A crust?

rule h7_bark_death_recent
when concept=bark world.death=recent here.place=street|chapel
cooldown 1d
say Gods rest them. | Quiet street today. | Still can't believe it. | The bell's still in my ears.

rule h7_bark_crime_nervy
when concept=bark world.crime=recent temper=nervy
cooldown 6h
say Who's that? Oh. Just a cat. | Is that my purse? It's my purse. Good. | I'll be home before the lamps. Before. | Don't look behind. Don't look behind.

rule h7_bark_owes_lender
when concept=bark owes=yes here.place=street|market
cooldown 1d
say If that's the lender, I'm not here. | Head down. Head down. Walk. | Restday. I'll pay Restday. Or the next. | Not that way. They live that way.
